Keep each RAGFlow dataset's GraphRAG graph in an embedded HawDB database.

RAGFlow v0.27.3, commit 8090ffd8ba6098813d7f7ec2c4b8774f36c8423a. The files this
patch changes are the same on the v0.27.x branch at commit
27847b3b9424d79140486e2142284319f4f71247.

Apply it from the root of a RAGFlow checkout:

    git apply /path/to/ragflow-v0.27.3.patch

Then install ragflow-hawdb and set hawdb_graph.path in conf/service_conf.yaml.
Without that setting, the patched RAGFlow keeps the graph in its document engine.

